  "worked_solution": "Since we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{\u2032}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =15-(-1) \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{\u2032}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31}=\\frac{1}{-4}\\cdot 16=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
